# Public Repository

This repository is public. Anything committed is visible to everyone, and
git history is permanent. Never commit private material.

Do not commit:

- Secrets: API keys, tokens, passwords, private keys, certificates,
  `.env` files, service account credentials
- Personal data: real user emails, phone numbers, addresses, device
  identifiers, account IDs, or real user content
- Private infrastructure detail: internal hostnames, IP addresses,
  non-public endpoints
- Internal-only documents: security audits, incident reports, unpublished
  business or legal material

Instead:

- Use obvious placeholders (`EXAMPLE_API_KEY`), `example.com` domains, and
  synthetic fixture data in code, tests, and docs
- Keep real values in untracked local files and make sure they are covered
  by `.gitignore`
- When unsure whether something is private, ask before committing it

Deleting a leaked value in a later commit does not undo the exposure. If
private material does reach the repo, say so immediately and treat the
value as compromised so it can be rotated.
